  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Emblem as Architecture",
    "overview": "The firm's gold emblem is not a logo placed on a page; it is the page's structure. On the public site the obsidian field carries the mark's own geometry at viewport scale: two gold uprights frame the content column, outer diagonals run to the corners, a faint chevron sits under the live decision, and a single gold diamond lands above the headline. Everything after the hero borrows from that vocabulary: gold hairline rules instead of boxes, rotated-square diamonds instead of bullets and icons, Cinzel capitals for every name the firm speaks in its own voice.\n\nThere are two scenes. **Persuade** (public pages) lives in the logo's world: obsidian ground with a faint warm grain, warm ivory reading text, gold reserved for structure, emphasis and action. **Operate** (the founder and advisor workspace) keeps an obsidian rail carrying the wordmark, then opens a light stone work area with white panels for daytime desk work, switching to a dark work area under `prefers-color-scheme: dark`. The workspace speaks in data: Hanken Grotesk, tabular numerals, three fixed series colours, and the gold diamond kept for the one recommended answer.\n\nDensity is calm on the public side (generous section padding, ruled ledgers, long measure capped at 62-72ch) and working-dense in the workspace (20px panel padding, 12-20px gaps, KPI rows). Motion is ceremonial exactly once, the Ascent on the home hero, and purely feedback everywhere else. The world refuses the fintech template: no light hero, no dashboard screenshot, no row of icon cards.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Obsidian ground, gold geometry, ivory text on public pages; stone and white panels in the workspace.",
      "Cinzel in spaced capitals for display, wordmark and section names; Hanken Grotesk for reading and data.",
      "Gold hairline rules (`gold-line`) as the main structural device; very few filled containers.",
      "The rotated-square diamond is the house marker: active place, chosen option, list bullet, recommended value.",
      "Every number is a dashed-underlined, clickable \"glass-box\" figure that opens its formula.",
      "One signature motion (the Ascent); workspace motion is 150-250ms feedback only."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Single Best Rule",
        "body": "In every chart and data view the gold diamond marks exactly one thing: the single \"Best\" point. Series markers, including the best-mix series' own markers, use their own series colour; a secondary \"Viewing\" mark is an ink-coloured diamond, never gold.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Gold Is Structure Rule",
        "body": "On dark pages gold appears as line, marker, numeral and action, never as a large fill. The largest gold areas are the primary button and the split bar's equity half.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Readable Gold Rule",
        "body": "On light surfaces gold text is always Deep Gold Ink (#7B5C1F), never Emblem Gold.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Cinzel Names, Hanken Explains Rule",
        "body": "Cinzel is for names, headings, numerals of the method and the wordmark; it never sets paragraphs, form labels or table cells.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every figure, in tables, KPIs, inputs and charts, sets in tabular lining numerals.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline Before Box Rule",
        "body": "Separate content with a 1px gold hairline first; reach for a filled panel only in the workspace, where panels hold working tools.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do build public pages on obsidian (#0D0E10) with ivory text and gold hairline rules (rgba(201,160,79,.28)) as the primary structure.",
      "Do set every name, heading and the wordmark in Cinzel 500 with positive tracking, and every paragraph, label and number in Hanken Grotesk.",
      "Do use the rotated-square diamond for markers, bullets, current-place and chosen-option states.",
      "Do keep the gold diamond in charts for the single \"Best\" mark; give every series marker its own series colour.",
      "Do colour debt, equity and mix with the fixed series palette (light #3F6EA6 / #B8892F / #1E8C68; dark #5C88C4 / #B08433 / #2FA38A).",
      "Do make figures clickable glass-box numbers with the dashed gold underline when they have a formula behind them.",
      "Do keep workspace motion to 150-250ms feedback and honour reduced motion everywhere."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't open with a light hero, a dashboard screenshot or a row of icon cards.",
      "Don't put a gold diamond on any chart point other than the one \"Best\" mark, and don't use gold as a series colour beyond Equity Gold.",
      "Don't set Emblem Gold (#C9A04F) as text on white; use Deep Gold Ink (#7B5C1F).",
      "Don't add drop shadows to panels or cards at rest, or round corners beyond 6px.",
      "Don't add a second ceremonial animation; the Ascent is the only one."
    ]
  }
